+# History of the trainers-week skill
+
+One entry per change, including the changes tried and dropped. Newest last.
+
+## 2026-10-31: first version, script and tests
+
+Status: kept.
+Why: every Friday, the planning team wants the trainers on duty the next week, Monday
+to Friday, day by day, with the warnings.
+What it does: `scripts/trainers_week.py` runs `planning.assign_trainers`, the board of
+`pachaplan trainers --date`, for each working day of the week after the reference date,
+prints each board with its warnings, then the warning count of the week per day.
+`Skill(trainers-week)` is not yet in the allow rules of `.claude/settings.json`: the
+change was refused to the session that wrote the skill, and is left to a person.
+Tests: 7 in `tests/test_trainers_week_skill.py`. Each of five broken copies of the
+script (wrong Monday, four days, week count at 0, `PACHAPLAN_TODAY` ignored, boards not
+printed) made at least one of them fail.
+Effect: not yet tried in a fresh `claude -p` session.
